From cdf1d9afda94e59f6a274db7b0d3f7dca00029b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 18:39:34 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Traffic Analyzer: Guest Portal panel, removed networks, idle
 rows, guest uploads (102.8 line)

- A Guest Portal panel on the Live tab: each signed-in guest with their speed and session time,
  busiest first; the portal's share as dashed lines on the total chart and a Guest Portal row in
  By network. Shown only while a portal runs.
- A network that has been removed leaves the live By network view; the traffic it carried stays in
  the history.
- A chosen timeframe lists only the devices that moved traffic in it.
- The flow-cache pass takes the guest bridges and the portal tunnels' subnets as LAN sources, so
  an accelerated guest upload is no longer also counted as the router's own traffic.
- A bar is the row's share of its list's total; the top row's bar was always full.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
